CPU PSUTIL Monitoring using Raspberry Pi

Aim

To monitor CPU usage and CPU count using the psutil library and control an LED using Raspberry Pi.

Components Required

- Raspberry Pi 4B
- LED
- Resistor
- Jumper wires

Software Requirements

- Python 3
- psutil library
- gpiozero library

Working

- The psutil library monitors CPU usage.
- "psutil.cpu_percent(interval=1)" checks CPU usage percentage.
- "psutil.cpu_count()" displays the number of CPU cores.
- The LED connected to GPIO 17 turns ON and OFF continuously.

Execution

Run the program using:

"python3 psutil_cpu.py"

Output

- LED ON
- CPU Usage percentage
- CPU Count
- LED OFF
- CPU Usage percentage
- CPU Count

Conclusion

CPU utilization is monitored successfully using the psutil library, and LED blinking is controlled using Raspberry Pi.
